ARDP: AMOC Reanalysis Diagnostic Pipeline
==========================================

Python code that computes Atlantic meridional overturning circulation (AMOC)
diagnostics from ocean reanalyses (ORAS5, GLORYS12V1, ECCO-V4r4, SODA 3.15.2),
the EN4 objective analysis of observed salinity and CMIP6 model output, and
produces every figure and number of the papers listed below.

License: MIT (see LICENSE).


Installation
------------

    pip install -e ".[dev]"

Dependencies: xarray, numpy, scipy, matplotlib, cartopy, xgcm, gsw,
copernicusmarine, intake. All data live under data/, which is not tracked;
the download scripts in scripts/ (download_*.py) retrieve them.


Overturning freshwater transport at 34.5 S (paper 3)
----------------------------------------------------

Run from the repository root, in this order. Every script caps its parallel
workers at four.

Trend, mean and correlation tests use scripts/paper3r1_stats.py: the effective
sample size is formed from the lag-1 autocorrelation of the regression
residuals corrected for its small-sample bias, intervals are the inverse of
the test, and shares of trends use a joint AR(1) sieve bootstrap. Running
    python scripts/paper3r1_stats.py
writes the simulated size of the test for the record lengths of the paper.

  1. Section fields (monthly velocity and salinity on the contiguous Atlantic
     section at 34.5 S):
         python scripts/extract_paper3r1_section_fields.py
  2. Section diagnostics (overturning and azonal freshwater transports, limb
     factorisation, streamfunction) for the baseline and the grid variants:
         python scripts/compute_paper3r1_section_quantities.py
  3. Attribution, frozen fields, observing-system steps, EN4 test and latitude
     sensitivity:
         python scripts/analysis_paper3v2_attribution.py
         python scripts/analysis_paper3v2_final_checks.py
         python scripts/analysis_paper3v2_stepfit.py
         python scripts/analysis_paper3v2_limb_composition.py
         python scripts/analysis_paper3v2_en4.py
         python scripts/analysis_paper3v2_en4_depth_test.py
         python scripts/analysis_paper3v2_latitude_sensitivity.py
  4. Overturning cells, common window, grid sensitivity, SAMBA comparison,
     salinity trend structure, CMIP6 and step-adjusted attribution:
         python scripts/analysis_paper3r1_cells.py
         python scripts/analysis_paper3r1_water_bodies.py
         python scripts/analysis_paper3r1_salinity_profiles.py
         python scripts/analysis_paper3r1_salinification_structure.py
         python scripts/analysis_paper3r1_cmip6.py
         python scripts/analysis_paper3r1_step_adjusted.py
         python scripts/analysis_paper3r1_rapid_trend.py
     The latitude sensitivity can refresh its statistics from the stored
     annual series without reading the reanalysis fields:
         python scripts/analysis_paper3v2_latitude_sensitivity.py --refresh-stats
  5. Figures of the Journal of Climate version, drawn at the printed width of
     39 pc with the shared style scripts/paper3jc_style.py; each writes a PDF
     and a 600 dpi PNG to PAPER_3_v2/figures_jclim/:
         Figure 1   scripts/plot_paper3jc_fig1_schematic.py
         Figure 2   scripts/plot_paper3jc_fig2_sign.py
         Figure 3   scripts/plot_paper3jc_fig3_attribution.py
         Figure 4   scripts/plot_paper3jc_fig4_salinification.py
         Figure 5   scripts/plot_paper3jc_fig5_en4.py
         Figure 6   scripts/plot_paper3jc_fig6_cells.py
         Figure 7   scripts/plot_paper3jc_fig7_models.py
     The colour palette and colour maps are shown by
         python scripts/paper3jc_swatch.py
     The earlier layouts of the same figures remain in
     scripts/plot_paper3r1_fig1_schematic.py to plot_paper3r1_fig7_models.py.
         Supplementary figures with SODA, trend sections, SAMBA, CMIP6
         trajectories, the pile-up index and the overturning anomalies at
         26.5 N:
                    scripts/plot_paper3r1_si_figures.py
         Supplementary surface salinity trends: scripts/plot_sss_trend_map.py
         Supplementary RAPID validation: scripts/plot_grl_figures.py
         Supplementary overturning strength against CMIP6:
                    scripts/plot_amoc_strength_comparison.py

The numbers in the text are read from the JSON summaries that steps 3 and 4
write to PAPER_3_v2/analysis/.


AMOC mechanisms (paper 2): figure to script mapping
---------------------------------------------------

Main text
  1  Mechanism-conditional AMOC projections, basin-mean salinity, F_ovS,
     Cold Blob                                   plot_paper2_Figure1.py
  2  Observational grounding: EN4 zonal section and upper-300 m salinity
     trends                                      plot_obs_grounding.py
  3  CMIP6 mechanism shares, mechanism-conditional AMOC, weakening by 2100
                                                 plot_paper2_Figure2.py
  4  AMOC projections restricted to the bistable subset
                                                 plot_paper2_Figure3.py
  5  Robustness: Argo-era windows, period sensitivity, piControl null
                                                 plot_paper2_Figure4.py
  6  Zonal structure of the velocity and salinity changes at 34.5 S
                                                 plot_paper2_Figure5.py
  7  Lead-lag, emergent regression, large-ensemble robustness
                                                 plot_paper2_Figure6.py

Supplementary
  S1 Within-class emergent regression test       diagnostic_a2_within_class_regression.py
  S2 Continuous velocity share against projected weakening
                                                 diagnostic_a3_continuous_correlation.py
  S3 Timescale consistency of the mechanism class
                                                 diagnostic_a1_timescale_consistency.py
  S4 Joint sensitivity to threshold and floor    diagnostic_a4_joint_sensitivity.py
  S5 Bootstrap distribution of the class-median gap
                                                 diagnostic_a5_gap_bootstrap.py
  S6 Permutation null for the mechanism-class label
                                                 robustness_permutation_and_bootstrap.py
  S7 Lead-lag cross-correlation by mechanism class
                                                 plot_paper2_figS1_leadlag.py
  S8 Salinity component against projected AMOC weakening
                                                 analysis_r1_salinity_amoc_coupling.py
  S9 Observation-constrained salinity-driven component
                                                 plot_obs_hybrid_dfs.py

Tables
  2  Net volume transport                        compute_paper2_tableS2_vnet.py
  S1 Model selection                             compute_paper2_tableS1.py


Other diagnostics
-----------------

  AMOC strength at 26.5 N:    scripts/compute_yearly_amoc26n.py, then
                              scripts/plot_amoc_strength_comparison.py
  Reanalysis AMOC anomalies:  scripts/compute_reanalysis_amoc.py, then
                              scripts/plot_amoc_reanalysis_anomalies.py
  F_ovS time series:          scripts/compute_oras5_fovs.py,
                              scripts/compute_cmip6_fovs_timeseries.py


Development
-----------

    ruff check .
    ruff format .
    mypy ardp/
    pytest tests/ -v

Package layout: ardp/ingestion (data loaders), ardp/physics (density,
freshwater transport, heat transport, streamfunction), ardp/fingerprints,
ardp/spatial (region masks), ardp/constants.py, ardp/viz; scripts/ holds the
download, compute, analysis and plotting scripts.
